From: Jean-Michael Celerier <jmcelerier@sat.qc.ca>
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rhi: gl: honour QRhiTexture::sRGB for uncompressed formats

QRhiTexture::sRGB reached the OpenGL backend only through
toGlCompressedTextureFormat(), i.e. for BC / ETC2 / ASTC, and through the
swapchain. toGlTextureFormat() maps RGBA8 to GL_RGBA8 unconditionally, so on an
uncompressed texture the flag was accepted and silently dropped: the sampler
returned the stored values with no sRGB->linear decode, while Vulkan, Metal and
D3D all decode.

Anything sampling an 8-bit colour texture is then too bright on OpenGL alone,
and not by a constant: the sRGB curve lifts mid-tones far more than its fixed
points at 0.0 and 1.0, so the error shows up as a hue shift rather than a gain
change. Measured on a glTF base-colour texture whose albedo is exactly
(1.0, 0.847, 0.0): the effective linear green a renderer sees is 0.687 on
Vulkan and Metal -- the decoded value -- and 0.847 on OpenGL, the raw one,
while red and blue agree to within 1/255 across all three because they sit on
the fixed points.

Map RGBA8 and BGRA8 to GL_SRGB8_ALPHA8 when the flag is set, and pass the
texture's flags down from QGles2Texture::create(). There is no sRGB BGRA
internal format, which is fine: the sRGB-ness belongs to the internal format
and BGRA stays the client-side channel order. Gated on caps.rgba8Format, i.e.
sized internal formats, since the unsized sRGB enums are not worth the ES2
special cases.

The two other call sites keep the default (no flags): one reads back pixels and
uses only glformat/gltype, the other resolves a renderbuffer's sized internal
format, and a QRhiRenderBuffer carries no sRGB flag.

diff --git a/src/gui/rhi/qrhigles2.cpp b/src/gui/rhi/qrhigles2.cpp
--- a/src/gui/rhi/qrhigles2.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/rhi/qrhigles2.cpp
@@ -214,6 +214,10 @@
 #define GL_R16                            0x822A
 #endif
 
+#ifndef GL_SRGB8_ALPHA8
+#define GL_SRGB8_ALPHA8                   0x8C43
+#endif
+
 #ifndef GL_RG16
 #define GL_RG16                           0x822C
 #endif
@@ -1489,18 +1493,28 @@
 
 static inline void toGlTextureFormat(QRhiTexture::Format format, const QRhiGles2::Caps &caps,
                                      GLenum *glintformat, GLenum *glsizedintformat,
-                                     GLenum *glformat, GLenum *gltype)
+                                     GLenum *glformat, GLenum *gltype,
+                                     QRhiTexture::Flags flags = {})
 {
+    // Only the sized sRGB internal format carries the decode; there is no
+    // unsized equivalent worth using, so this needs GL 3.0 / ES 3.0, which is
+    // what rgba8Format (GL_EXT_texture_storage / sized formats) stands for.
+    const bool srgb = flags.testFlag(QRhiTexture::sRGB) && caps.rgba8Format;
     switch (format) {
     case QRhiTexture::RGBA8:
-        *glintformat = GL_RGBA;
-        *glsizedintformat = caps.rgba8Format ? GL_RGBA8 : GL_RGBA;
+        *glintformat = srgb ? GL_SRGB8_ALPHA8 : GL_RGBA;
+        *glsizedintformat = srgb ? GL_SRGB8_ALPHA8
+                                 : (caps.rgba8Format ? GL_RGBA8 : GL_RGBA);
         *glformat = GL_RGBA;
         *gltype = GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE;
         break;
     case QRhiTexture::BGRA8:
-        *glintformat = caps.bgraInternalFormat ? GL_BGRA : GL_RGBA;
-        *glsizedintformat = caps.rgba8Format ? GL_RGBA8 : GL_RGBA;
+        // No sRGB BGRA internal format exists; the sRGB-ness lives in the
+        // internal format and BGRA stays the client-side channel order.
+        *glintformat = srgb ? GL_SRGB8_ALPHA8
+                            : (caps.bgraInternalFormat ? GL_BGRA : GL_RGBA);
+        *glsizedintformat = srgb ? GL_SRGB8_ALPHA8
+                                 : (caps.rgba8Format ? GL_RGBA8 : GL_RGBA);
         *glformat = GL_BGRA;
         *gltype = GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE;
         break;
@@ -6608,7 +6622,8 @@
         glformat = GL_RGBA;
     } else {
         toGlTextureFormat(m_format, rhiD->caps,
-                          &glintformat, &glsizedintformat, &glformat, &gltype);
+                          &glintformat, &glsizedintformat, &glformat, &gltype,
+                          m_flags);
     }
 
     samplerState = QGles2SamplerData();
